WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.197
ORDER BY inside OVER is part of the analytical definition.

00:00:04.197 --> 00:00:07.632
For ranking, it defines higher and lower positions.

00:00:07.632 --> 00:00:11.147
For LAG and LEAD, it defines previous and next.

00:00:11.147 --> 00:00:14.857
For running totals, it defines the sequence of accumulation.

00:00:14.857 --> 00:00:21.237
When ordering values can tie, add a stable tie-breaker when deterministic row sequence matters.

00:00:21.237 --> 00:00:26.232
Window functions preserve detail rows while calculating across a related set.

00:00:26.232 --> 00:00:29.217
PARTITION BY defines independent groups, ORDER BY defines sequence,

00:00:29.217 --> 00:00:34.452
and the frame defines which neighboring rows participate.

00:00:34.452 --> 00:00:38.101
Those three choices are part of the business rule, not just syntax.
